  "display_title": "Keep cached root parameters out of generic fallback shells",
  "event": "pull_request",
  "head_branch": "codex/root-param-shell-cache",
  "head_commit": {
    "author": {
      "email": "gnoff@storyposted.com",
      "name": "Josh Story"
    },
    "committer": {
      "email": "gnoff@storyposted.com",
      "name": "Josh Story"
    },
    "id": "859b040cdc7b407a5937dee8af10ddcf79eeb195",
    "message": "Track fallback root access only when cached promises are consumed\n\nUse a single promise-tracking wrapper for unknown root getters and aborted cache fills. Wrapping an already tracked promise invokes its then method while constructing the outer wrapper, recording fallback access before a consumer actually awaits the value. Keep access tracking and cache cancellation together in the consumption callback instead.\n\nFor example, a cached helper that calls lang() but does not consume the returned promise should not record fallback access solely because the promise was constructed. Preserve root dependency collection and per-consumer cancellation, and make the enclosing-prerender selection explicit without changing abort classification or RDC reuse.\n\nVerified package types, lint, the five promise-tracking unit tests, and the three production fallback-root cache tests.",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-20T02:43:54Z",
    "tree_id": "0a725f2f3d3694278a959baa432da114e48a2747"
  },
